<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spanish conquest of the Aztec Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1519">1519</a>–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spanish conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> was the campaign led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a> from 1519 to 1521, in alliance with Indigenous peoples such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlaxcalans">Tlaxcalans</a>. It ended with the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>. The Aztec Empire and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> profiles note the role of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> in weakening the Aztecs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-conquest-of-the-aztec-empire.jpg" alt="Spanish conquest of the Aztec Empire" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conquista-de-M%C3%A9xico-por-Cort%C3%A9s-Tenochtitlan-Painting.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
